A||||5||p4n1c||Oil Pump revisited||||1||
Z||000000||p4n1c||01-27-2001||09:30 AM||||Sorry for the O/T this isn't for a Fiero, but it's about the 2.8 in my parents car.  My dad has some questions about the oil pump and possible causes of the guage dropping at idle.<P>The pump has been replaced and oil is getting to the engine, there is no noise coming from the engine(no knocking), and next to no filings were in the old pump which they were told was normal.  The sensor however was not replaced, could this be the cause?  Dad is a little ticked that they told him that it might be the oil pump got it replaced and that wasn't it.<P>Any help is appreciated.<BR><P>------------------<BR>-=-=-=[ p4n1c ]=-=-=-<BR>"Each passing day, every passing face seems like such a blur" <BR>- The Offspring(Million Miles Away)||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||01-27-2001||12:39 PM||||install a cheap mecahnical gauge and make sure of what it is really doing. the electric one can screw up in a number of ways.||||reg||1
Z||000002||DJRice||01-28-2001||11:54 PM||||You say the gauge drops a bit at idle...it should, and your system may not have been operating normally before.  Because the oil pumps are mechanical the oil PSI will vary with engine RPM so low RPM=Low PSI and higher RPM=higher PSI.  Typically you should see 30-40psi at idle and about 70psi at highway crusing speeds.  <P>However, as ogre said, the only way to be sure is a good ol' mechanical gauge.  <P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR>"You mean like the back seat of a Volkswagen?"||||reg||1
Z||000003||p4n1c||01-29-2001||11:51 AM||||A bit is an understatement.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  It actually drops to 0.  The digital dash starts going nuts with the low light.  That's what made us believe it's just the sensor on the car.<P>------------------<BR>-=-=-=[ p4n1c ]=-=-=-<BR>"Each passing day, every passing face seems like such a blur" <BR>- The Offspring(Million Miles Away)||||reg||1
Z||000004||88formula||01-29-2001||06:56 PM|||| Do what theogre says. Those GM gauges are never accurate.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Cooter||01-29-2001||07:07 PM||||When my Mom's new Cavalier with the digital dash was on it's way home from the dealership with less than 20 miles on it, the guage dropped to zero. Turned out to be the sending unit, but even then it only held the first two bars on the guage at idle.||||reg||1
